### ClearWood Furnitures — Catalog hardening (relationships, contract work, scoped imports)
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.
### Nothing here needs a deploy: relations, categories and imports are data an admin changes.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Sign in (sets cw_adm_at / cw_adm_rt / cw_adm_csrf)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@clearwood.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe@12345"
}

###
@csrf = {{adminLogin.response.headers.$['set-cookie'][2]}}

# @name twoProducts
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products?publication=LIVE&limit=3

###
@hostId = {{twoProducts.response.body.data.0.id}}
@hostSlug = {{twoProducts.response.body.data.0.slug}}
@otherId = {{twoProducts.response.body.data.1.id}}
@thirdId = {{twoProducts.response.body.data.2.id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------ relationships

### 2. Replace the host's curated relations. One product may appear under several types; the
###    order inside a type is `position`. SIMILAR is mirrored onto the other product.
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{hostId}}/relations
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "relations": [
    { "relatedProductId": "{{otherId}}", "type": "RELATED", "position": 0 },
    { "relatedProductId": "{{thirdId}}", "type": "ALTERNATIVE", "position": 0 },
    { "relatedProductId": "{{otherId}}", "type": "COMPLEMENTARY", "position": 1 },
    { "relatedProductId": "{{thirdId}}", "type": "FREQUENTLY_BOUGHT", "position": 0 },
    { "relatedProductId": "{{otherId}}", "type": "SIMILAR", "position": 0 }
  ]
}

### 3. 422: the same product twice under one type (details.repeated lists the pairs)
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{hostId}}/relations
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "relations": [
    { "relatedProductId": "{{otherId}}", "type": "RELATED", "position": 0 },
    { "relatedProductId": "{{otherId}}", "type": "RELATED", "position": 1 }
  ]
}

### 4. 422: a product cannot relate to itself (a deleted target is refused the same way)
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{hostId}}/relations
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "relations": [{ "relatedProductId": "{{hostId}}", "type": "RELATED" }] }

### 5. The PDP: relationGroups in type order, then related / frequentlyBoughtTogether as before.
###    Hidden, draft, scheduled and deleted products never appear in any of them.
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{hostSlug}}

### 6. Exactly one curated type; an empty list when none is curated (never the category fallback)
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{hostSlug}}/related?type=ALTERNATIVE

### 7. Without a type: every curated type except FREQUENTLY_BOUGHT, else the category's best sellers
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{hostSlug}}/related

### ------------------------------------------------------------ contract work

### 8. The tree says which categories are service lines and which form they open
GET {{api}}/catalog/categories/tree

### 9. A service landing: kind SERVICE, leadFormKey "contract-work", no products, children alike
GET {{api}}/catalog/categories/contract-based-work/landing

# @name serviceCategory
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/categories/tree

### 10. 422 CATEGORY_NOT_PURCHASABLE: a product is never filed under a service category
###     (replace the id with custom-hotel-furniture's id from the tree above)
PUT {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{hostId}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "primaryCategoryId": "REPLACE_WITH_SERVICE_CATEGORY_ID", "categoryIds": [] }

### 11. The enquiry itself (rate-limited per client, honeypot `website` stored as SPAM)
POST {{api}}/enquiries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "formKey": "contract-work",
  "categorySlug": "custom-hotel-furniture",
  "name": "Asha Rao",
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "quantity": 40,
  "details": { "rooms": 40 }
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------ scoped import invalidation

### 12. A dry run (the default) writes nothing and invalidates nothing
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/PRODUCT
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cw

--cw
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="products.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

sku,basePriceRupees
REPLACE_WITH_A_SKU,12345
--cw--

### 13. Committed, it drops the product payloads (listings, PDPs, facets, suggestions, CMS pages,
###     quotes) and re-prices and re-indexes exactly the imported products; navigation, settings,
###     category-attribute and CMS FAQ/banner caches stay warm. Counts follow a moved category link.
POST {{api}}/admin/catalog/import/PRODUCT
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cw

--cw
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="dryRun"

false
--cw
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="products.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

sku,basePriceRupees
REPLACE_WITH_A_SKU,12345
--cw--
